      ],
      "content": "KINGS LANGLEY          \tBARNES LANE TL 00 SE  \t\t\t\t\t(North side)                                       7/118                                   \tNorth Barn at -                                      \t\tBarnes Farm                                         \t(10m to W of house) GV                                      \tII Barn. C17. Timber frame dark weatherboarded with steep old red tile roof carried down over S aisle. A tall 5 bays single aisled barn with gabled porch in middle of S aisle with pidgeon loft in gable. Stepped jowl posts with straight braces to tie-beams and arcade plate. Mid-height rails in walls in-line. 45° pitched roof with collar trusses and struts across lower angles. Side-purlin roof, the upper purlin clasped with diminished principals, the lower butt purlins staggered in line, with straight wind braces.  Aisle purlin propped by inclined strut from aisle-tie. Squint-butted scarf joint with 2 edge pegs in arcade plate. Modern entrance at W end. (The farmhouse at Barnes Farm is not listed). Listing NGR: TL0616003460"
    }
